<headroom-library version="1" id="crunch-british-blues-boom" category="Crunch" order="60" instrument="guitar" style="Blues Rock">
  <description>Mid-60s London blues at full volume: humbuckers into a 2x12 combo of the early British-amp lineage with both channels up, no pedals. Thick, woody and singing, with a round mid push. Neck pickup with the tone rolled back for sweet leads, bridge for biting riffs.</description>
  <tags><tag>Crunch</tag><tag>Blues Rock</tag><tag>Blues</tag><tag>No pedals</tag><tag>Humbucker</tag><tag>Lead</tag></tags>
  <sources>
    <source url="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blues_Breakers_with_Eric_Clapton" title="Blues Breakers with Eric Clapton (Wikipedia)"/>
    <source url="https://guitar.com/features/guitar-legends-eric-clapton-part-1/" title="Guitar.com: Guitar Legends, Eric Clapton part 1"/>
    <source url="https://www.musicradar.com/news/when-he-felt-the-spirit-he-was-untouchable-the-story-of-bluesbreakers-with-eric-clapton-and-peter-green" title="MusicRadar: the story of Bluesbreakers with Eric Clapton and Peter Green"/>
    <source url="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marshall_Bluesbreaker" title="Marshall Bluesbreaker (Wikipedia)"/>
  </sources>
</headroom-library>
